  [TSPB], cell("52715.58", "51045 – 54785", 0.00), cell("0.0365", "0.0302 – 0.0576", 0.00),
  table.cell(rowspan: 2)[steepest + LM],
  [TSPA], cell("76095.35", "73770 – 79340", -0.02), cell("0.0022", "0.0016 – 0.0065", -93.92),
  [TSPB], cell("52555.36", "50011 – 54876", -0.30), cell("0.0020", "0.0015 – 0.0028", -94.52),
)

The cached variant is *not slower and not worse*: average objective is marginally better on both instances (−0.02% and −0.30%, i.e. inside the run-to-run noise of the two searches exploring different move orders) while the average runtime drops from ~36 ms to ~2 ms per run, a reduction of about 94%. The best solutions found are also better or comparable (TSPA 73770 vs 73595, TSPB 50011 vs 51045 — the LM run wins clearly on TSPB).

